From c1b27400ad0767e643d17365835d6e4dd3e5d257 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:52:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 029/102] feat(routing): classify against a registered router
 in /routing/validate

POST /routing/validate now also accepts {"model": <collection.router>, ...}
and returns the decision that router's registered policy makes for the
request body, without dispatching or loading any candidate. The decision
comes from the same evaluation path dispatch uses (split out of
route_collection_request minus its routing-metrics side effect), so validate
and dispatch cannot disagree.

The ad-hoc policy mode is unchanged. Sending both 'policy' and 'model' is
rejected with 400; an unknown model is 404 and a non-router model is 400.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
